     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi<div>Is it possible to change the color of points in each box plots in the box and outside of the box :</div><div><ul><li>from black to red if Recrutement == Cad (exemple : all the points of 6-7C in red but visible)<br></li><li>from black to  blue if Recrutement == NonCad (exemple : all the points of 1-2 in blue but visible)<br></li></ul></div><div>My code is  </div><div><div>p &lt;- ggplot(Test, aes(x=factor(Cat1), y=AgeChangCat )) +</div><div>geom_point()  + <br></div><div>geom_boxplot(aes(fill = Recrutement)) +</div><div>scale_fill_manual(values = alpha(c(&quot;red&quot;, &quot;blue&quot;),0.5)) +</div><div>labs(title = &quot;Age&quot;,</div><div>x=&quot;Passage de i à i+1&quot;, y=&quot;Age&quot;,</div><div>fill = &quot;Classification au\\nrecrutement&quot;) +</div><div>theme(legend.position = c(0.12,0.9),</div><div>legend.background = element_rect(colour = &quot;black&quot;)) </div><div>p</div></div><div><br></div><div>an exemple in the file</div><div>The reproductible exemple is </div><div>Test &lt;- structure(list(AgeChangCat = c(53.2, 50.7, 51.5, 44.2, 45.7, </div><div>56.9, 42.2, 45.7, 55.5, 43.6, 62.6, 43.1, 39.2, 55.2, 37, 42.3, </div><div>48.4, 35.2, 44.2, 50.1, 39.4, 53.4, 33.5, 42.8, 56.4, 45.8, 42.4, </div><div>58.8, 45.2, 42.6, 51.4, 43.9, 35.1, 52, 39.1, 53.9, 50.5, 37.1, </div><div>49.3, 42.9, 37.7, 43.7, 53.7, 54.9, 37, 42.3, 55.5, 44.4, 56.5, </div><div>32.7, 45.9, 41.2, 40.1, 50.1, 36.7, 54.4, 37.4, 46.4, 41.8, 41.1, </div><div>45.6, 52.9, 41.1, 50.2, 49.5, 45.1, 33.1, 39.1, 47.6, 52.1, 47.9, </div><div>53.9, 44, 53, 36.5, 49.7, 29.2, 39.8, 48.8, 57.3, 49.6, 39.8, </div><div>45.9, 42.7, 47.8, 30.9, 36, 46.9, 55.5, 56.6, 51.2, 35.4, 44.6, </div><div>51.8, 43.3, 37.7, 50.9, 53.1, 48.3, 47.7, 60.3, 37.8, 49.1, 33.5, </div><div>56.9, 36.8, 40.3, 29.9, 41, 55, 36.8, 55, 40.6, 56.4, 51.9, 29.3, </div><div>38, 45.5, 33.1, 47.8, 33.8, 49.3, 38.6, 50.9, 38.2, 44.2, 52.9, </div><div>36.8, 35.4, 47.7, 46.2, 32.3, 53.2, 54, 38.3, 45